# Changelog

Notable changes to Wrong Boot (wrong8007).

## 0.1.0 (2026-11-10)

This release moves trigger selection to Kconfig and trigger values to a root-only parameter file, runs the payload without a shell and fixes the bugs found along the way.

### Configuration

* Kconfig build profiles that choose which triggers are compiled into the module (`make menuconfig`, `configs/defconfig`)
* Load parameters in `/etc/wrong8007/wrong8007.conf` with mode `0600` (`make params-init`, `make params-check`, `make load-installed`)
* Parameters in `/etc/wrong8007/wrong8007.conf` outside modprobe.d and the initramfs
* Debug lines that never log a secret
* Helper tools to check the build profile and parameter file against the build
* A build with no trigger refused at compile time

### Payload execution

* Payload executed directly instead of through `/bin/sh -c`
* Absolute `exec` path required at load
* Own workqueue for the payload and its retries
* Payload start and failure to start in the kernel log
* Retry with backoff for a payload that fails to start
* No second run for a payload that started
* Unload that never waits for a running payload

### Triggers

* Keyboard matching on the characters the kernel resolves from each key press
* Knuth-Morris-Pratt phrase matcher (`lib/phrase_match.c`)
* Strict USB rule and MAC address parsing (`lib/parse.c`)
* Hardened packet parsing in the network trigger
* Netfilter hook registered only when a network condition is set

### Tooling

* `wrong8007ctl` with `send`, `heartbeat` and `usb-list` in place of the Python and shell helpers
* CI build of every trigger profile against kernels 5.4 to 7.2

### Fixes

* Phrase with a repeated beginning missed (`aab` typed as `aaab`)
* Port-only network trigger that never fired
* Empty string parameter (`match_mac=`) that stopped the module from loading
* Trigger phrase written to the kernel log at load and keysyms logged in debug builds
* Reject out-of-range `match_port` values at module load
* Use-after-free on failed load and activation during a partial init
* Build on Linux 7.2 where `hex_to_bin()` moved to `<linux/hex.h>`
* Payload offsets computed relative to `skb->data`
* Duplicated `wrong8007:` prefix in a log line
* Failed load that could leave the payload work queued after the module was freed
* Activation accepted while later triggers were still loading

### Breaking changes

* `make load PHRASE=... EXEC=...` removed. Put the values in `/etc/wrong8007/wrong8007.conf`.
* Shell commands no longer accepted as `exec`. Point it at an executable file.
* Malformed USB rules and MAC addresses refused at load instead of partly read.
* `scripts/` helpers removed. Use `wrong8007ctl`.

## 0.0.1 (2025-12-19)

First tagged release of the kernel module rewrite.

### Core

* Pluggable trigger interface where triggers report a condition and the core owns execution
* Fail-closed initialization that unwinds in reverse order on a partial failure
* One-shot execution held by an atomic latch
* Payload run from a workqueue through the usermode helper

### Triggers

* Keyboard phrase matching under a spinlock in notifier context
* USB rules (`VID:PID[:EVENT]`) for several devices with whitelist and blacklist modes
* Network matching on source MAC, source IPv4, TCP or UDP port and payload string
* Heartbeat timer as a dead man's switch

### Project

* `make load`, `make remove` and `make reload`
* Logging macros, SPDX headers and GPL-2.0 for `EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL` compatibility
* CI build workflows with issue and pull request templates
* Design philosophy, security model, development guide and data destruction notes
* Example wipe payload

### Fixes

* Kernel crash from running the helper in atomic context
* `skb` header checks and a payload size underflow on malformed packets
* Separate parsing state for `match_ip` and `heartbeat_host`
* Spaces kept in string module parameters
* Negative key values guarded
